1
00:00:04,109 --> 00:00:08,363
ONE MONTH AGO

2
00:00:09,865 --> 00:00:11,617
[bell dinging]

3
00:00:13,327 --> 00:00:17,331
KANYARAK BOONSI BORN 1988.09.25
DIED 2017.12.17

4
00:00:46,276 --> 00:00:48,195
[Pasin, in Thai]
Why are you eating only that?

5
00:00:48,278 --> 00:00:49,655
You should eat everything!

6
00:00:49,738 --> 00:00:51,031
Mom is watching everything.

7
00:00:55,243 --> 00:00:56,328
Hm!

8
00:00:57,162 --> 00:00:58,455
You're the same, Dad.

9
00:00:58,538 --> 00:00:59,873
You should eat everything.

10
00:01:03,627 --> 00:01:07,923
Dad, let's stop listening to this song.
I'm sick of it.

11
00:01:08,632 --> 00:01:10,550
Why? I want to listen to it.

12
00:01:10,634 --> 00:01:13,220
-Let's listen to Lisa.
-K-pop?

13
00:01:13,845 --> 00:01:17,724
Lisa is not K-pop. Now she's a world star.

14
00:01:18,350 --> 00:01:20,894
You listen to her every day at home too.
Aren't you sick of it?

15
00:01:21,645 --> 00:01:23,563
I'm more sick of your song.

16
00:01:24,064 --> 00:01:25,065
You want to get off?

17
00:01:27,484 --> 00:01:29,069
[Pasin] Long time no see!

18
00:01:31,363 --> 00:01:34,074
[♪ bright upbeat music from radio]

19
00:01:45,168 --> 00:01:47,629
Lisa followed me around every day
when I was in Korea.

20
00:01:47,879 --> 00:01:50,298
[Pasin's son] Oh! You're lying again.
You're such a liar!

21
00:01:51,591 --> 00:01:53,009
You want me to call her?

22
00:01:53,093 --> 00:01:58,765
Yeah, call her. I said, call her.
Call her now. Yeah, call her.

23
00:02:03,603 --> 00:02:05,480
[vehicles approaching]

24
00:02:10,318 --> 00:02:12,404
[♪ ominous music playing]

25
00:02:29,171 --> 00:02:31,256
[♪ intense action music playing]

26
00:02:31,339 --> 00:02:33,383
[both grunting]

27
00:02:42,642 --> 00:02:44,436
[both grunting]

28
00:02:44,519 --> 00:02:45,604
[thuds]

29
00:02:52,194 --> 00:02:53,653
[mercenary] Go! Go! Go!

30
00:02:54,196 --> 00:02:56,406
[♪ intense action music continues]

31
00:03:04,122 --> 00:03:05,707
[thuds]

32
00:03:10,295 --> 00:03:13,340
[in English] Hey, we need to borrow
your dad for a bit.

33
00:03:14,132 --> 00:03:16,259
[Pasin's son breathing shakily]

34
00:03:17,761 --> 00:03:18,762
[in Thai] It's okay.

35
00:03:20,472 --> 00:03:22,891
Don't be scared, Atti.

36
00:03:26,520 --> 00:03:33,527
A SHOP FOR KILLERS 2

37
00:03:37,531 --> 00:03:39,950
EPISODE 06
THE TROJAN HORSE

38
00:03:40,033 --> 00:03:44,246
[announcer, in English]
Three-nine, two-zero, five-zero,

39
00:03:45,038 --> 00:03:47,749
seven-seven, three-four…

40
00:03:48,333 --> 00:03:49,334
[Jinman] K.

41
00:03:51,878 --> 00:03:54,923
[♪ tense music playing]
STYLE
::cue()

42
00:03:55,006 --> 00:03:57,425
WILL ARRIVE AT 11:00 AM LOCAL TIME
IN THAILAND, CONTACT PASIN.

43
00:03:57,509 --> 00:04:00,011
REQUEST ATTI'S LOCATION AND
THE KIDNAPPERS' INFORMATION BY 11:00

44
00:04:00,136 --> 00:04:02,764
[sighs] This is how the mole e-mails.

45
00:04:04,224 --> 00:04:05,892
When I'm in Thailand,
I'll be communicating

46
00:04:05,976 --> 00:04:07,060
with the mole like this,

47
00:04:07,143 --> 00:04:08,645
so verify the information.

48
00:04:09,771 --> 00:04:11,147
[Jinwoo] That wasn't easy.

49
00:04:12,274 --> 00:04:15,360
But it came out nicely.
Passport and satellite phone.

50
00:04:15,443 --> 00:04:16,778
REPUBLIC OF KOREA PASSPORT
CHOI, MYUNG GYU

51
00:04:16,861 --> 00:04:18,488
What's this? You're going in alone?

52
00:04:19,573 --> 00:04:21,616
You're not going to take Jinwoo
or Cheolseung in there?

53
00:04:22,492 --> 00:04:25,620
Hey, it's Pasin.
The two of us together will be fine.

54
00:04:26,746 --> 00:04:27,831
I just…

55
00:04:27,914 --> 00:04:29,249
Think about it, Jeong Jian.

56
00:04:30,083 --> 00:04:31,459
We made our deal already,

57
00:04:31,543 --> 00:04:33,461
but they still went ahead
and grabbed his son.

58
00:04:33,545 --> 00:04:35,964
That means Babylon's planning
something else.

59
00:04:36,715 --> 00:04:39,009
If the shopping mall's unguarded
while we're away,

60
00:04:39,092 --> 00:04:41,011
they might use that opening to attack.

61
00:04:41,094 --> 00:04:43,346
We need to leave some of you behind.

62
00:04:45,724 --> 00:04:46,766
[satellite phone beeps]

63
00:04:48,059 --> 00:04:50,353
[Cheolseung] This satellite phone
doesn't have a delay, does it?

64
00:04:50,437 --> 00:04:52,814
[Jinwoo] No, it works right away.
Only on this channel.

65
00:04:53,481 --> 00:04:56,067
[♪ tense music continues]

66
00:05:03,658 --> 00:05:05,410
Are you sure about going alone like this?

67
00:05:06,745 --> 00:05:08,997
[sighs] Don't you think it's safer
if I tagged along?

68
00:05:09,080 --> 00:05:12,125
No, stay here.
Jian's going to need you more with her.

69
00:05:15,629 --> 00:05:17,213
[engine revving]

70
00:05:34,522 --> 00:05:35,732
[sighs softly]

71
00:05:37,275 --> 00:05:38,443
[Jinman] Listen up, Jeong Jian.

72
00:05:39,736 --> 00:05:42,364
There could be a situation
where you lose an arm.

73
00:05:44,032 --> 00:05:45,158
What happens then?

74
00:05:45,241 --> 00:05:47,035
Don't try to recover the arm you lost.

75
00:05:48,662 --> 00:05:50,705
You should protect the one you still have.

76
00:05:52,499 --> 00:05:54,960
[♪ tense music continues]

77
00:06:05,971 --> 00:06:07,764
[engine starting, revving]

78
00:06:30,912 --> 00:06:32,872
[♪ low pensive music playing]

79
00:07:10,410 --> 00:07:13,413
[Pasin] Khao Lak Center,
locker number eight.

80
00:07:14,289 --> 00:07:17,250
Password is 2-4-5-1.

81
00:07:19,252 --> 00:07:20,920
You can find a device inside.

82
00:07:22,213 --> 00:07:24,716
The coordinates will take you
to an Internet café.

83
00:07:25,967 --> 00:07:27,302
I'll meet you there.

84
00:07:28,803 --> 00:07:31,514
[♪ tense music playing]

85
00:07:41,816 --> 00:07:43,443
[phone clattering]
STYLE
::cue()

86
00:08:05,048 --> 00:08:06,216
[♪ music fades]

87
00:08:06,299 --> 00:08:09,385
[indistinct chatter]

88
00:08:13,807 --> 00:08:15,767
[in Thai] Pay later. Sit.
You can use the seat over there.

89
00:08:16,267 --> 00:08:17,560
-[Jinman] There?
-Yeah.

90
00:08:23,483 --> 00:08:25,527
Hey! Why are you cheating?

91
00:08:25,610 --> 00:08:28,321
[gamer] What cheating? You crazy bastard.

92
00:08:29,072 --> 00:08:31,866
[indistinct chatter continues]

93
00:08:58,476 --> 00:09:01,104
[drone buzzing]

94
00:09:12,031 --> 00:09:14,659
[♪ low tense music playing]

95
00:09:16,995 --> 00:09:19,831
[patrons complaining indistinctly]

96
00:09:30,425 --> 00:09:33,636
[blade scraping]

97
00:09:48,943 --> 00:09:52,197
[attackers grunting]

98
00:09:57,702 --> 00:09:59,579
[screams]

99
00:10:03,082 --> 00:10:05,877
[♪ low suspenseful music playing]

100
00:10:07,337 --> 00:10:08,713
[attackers yelping]

101
00:10:16,054 --> 00:10:17,180
It's just him anyway.

102
00:10:18,723 --> 00:10:19,724
Get him!

103
00:10:20,016 --> 00:10:22,352
[attackers screaming]

104
00:10:26,940 --> 00:10:30,818
[Pasin panting]

105
00:10:36,241 --> 00:10:38,117
[groans]

106
00:10:48,711 --> 00:10:50,463
[glass shatters]

107
00:10:58,179 --> 00:11:00,598
[♪ tense music playing]

108
00:11:04,060 --> 00:11:06,604
[taser zapping]

109
00:11:15,071 --> 00:11:17,657
-[taser zapping]
-[groans softly]

110
00:11:23,371 --> 00:11:26,082
[mercenary whistling]

111
00:11:29,836 --> 00:11:31,713
[in English] Whoa… Two of them.

112
00:11:32,547 --> 00:11:33,715
Still holding out.

113
00:11:34,674 --> 00:11:36,801
Really haven't changed at all,
have you, Jinman?

114
00:11:37,802 --> 00:11:38,845
[bat thudding]

115
00:11:43,474 --> 00:11:45,935
[alarm beeping softly]

116
00:11:51,649 --> 00:11:52,650
Huh?

117
00:12:01,868 --> 00:12:03,077
[gasps]

118
00:12:07,999 --> 00:12:10,710
[♪ lingering ominous music playing]

119
00:12:19,427 --> 00:12:22,472
[Jin] Did you really think
that Babylon couldn't find you?

120
00:12:22,805 --> 00:12:25,725
-[blows thudding]
-[Pasin groaning]
STYLE
::cue()

121
00:12:30,563 --> 00:12:32,357
[Jin] I really do hate it.

122
00:12:34,484 --> 00:12:35,902
The smell of blood.

123
00:12:36,027 --> 00:12:37,362
[sniffs, groans in disgust]

124
00:12:37,528 --> 00:12:38,738
The smell of sweat.

125
00:12:40,406 --> 00:12:42,116
[roars angrily]

126
00:12:42,408 --> 00:12:44,952
I'll break your neck!

127
00:12:46,537 --> 00:12:50,541
Family… is always the problem.

128
00:12:51,918 --> 00:12:53,711
You know, in the past,

129
00:12:53,795 --> 00:12:57,632
they used to exterminate three generations

130
00:12:57,715 --> 00:13:00,718
just to prevent
any uncertain future revenge.

131
00:13:01,469 --> 00:13:03,763
Seems quite reasonable
when you think about it.

132
00:13:04,847 --> 00:13:06,849
But it's really too bad.

133
00:13:06,933 --> 00:13:08,434
People can't do that anymore.

134
00:13:08,518 --> 00:13:09,852
Where's Atti?

135
00:13:09,936 --> 00:13:11,062
[in Thai] You bitch!

136
00:13:11,312 --> 00:13:13,022
[shushing]

137
00:13:14,607 --> 00:13:16,567
[Pasin groans]

138
00:13:22,365 --> 00:13:25,493
[in English] Turns out your son
has leukemia.

139
00:13:26,119 --> 00:13:27,578
[Pasin grunts]

140
00:13:36,462 --> 00:13:38,798
[Jin] It's really remarkable.

141
00:13:39,465 --> 00:13:46,013
You poured all the money you made
for a decade into your son.

142
00:13:52,812 --> 00:13:53,813
[grunts]

143
00:14:01,279 --> 00:14:02,280
[spits]

144
00:14:06,242 --> 00:14:07,952
[Pasin] Babylon!

145
00:14:08,953 --> 00:14:10,371
You listen now.

146
00:14:11,914 --> 00:14:14,500
Anything happens to Atti…

147
00:14:16,961 --> 00:14:19,463
you all die.

148
00:14:20,339 --> 00:14:23,759
Do not waste your time
thinking about killing me.

149
00:14:24,302 --> 00:14:27,138
You should be thinking
about saving your son.

150
00:14:27,805 --> 00:14:29,891
[♪ ominous music playing]

151
00:14:31,225 --> 00:14:32,351
[gun cocking]

152
00:14:36,856 --> 00:14:38,357
[gunshot ringing]

153
00:14:38,941 --> 00:14:40,651
-[groans]
-[K] Good work.

154
00:14:41,235 --> 00:14:42,236
[Jin] Don't worry.

155
00:14:43,279 --> 00:14:45,323
We're taking good care of him.

156
00:14:49,827 --> 00:14:51,787
So in return…

157
00:14:53,164 --> 00:14:55,917
you are going to have to do
a little work for us.

158
00:14:57,084 --> 00:14:59,045
[groans]

159
00:15:06,093 --> 00:15:08,846
[howls in pain]

160
00:15:09,513 --> 00:15:10,973
[Pasin] Atti.

161
00:15:19,190 --> 00:15:20,816
So you're saying…

162
00:15:21,859 --> 00:15:23,736
you never met my uncle there, then?

163
00:15:24,737 --> 00:15:27,657
[♪ pensive music playing]

164
00:15:29,575 --> 00:15:30,993
-[staple gun clicking]
-[Pasin groans]

165
00:15:32,995 --> 00:15:33,996
Ah. Ah.

166
00:15:34,080 --> 00:15:36,999
-[K] Can you hear me?
-I hear you.

167
00:15:37,667 --> 00:15:39,043
Loud and clear.

168
00:15:43,589 --> 00:15:45,716
We are listening to everything you say.

169
00:15:46,884 --> 00:15:49,011
[Jin] Don't try anything fucking stupid.

170
00:15:50,388 --> 00:15:54,016
If you do, your Atti won't be safe.

171
00:15:56,602 --> 00:15:58,771
About 12 hours ago,

172
00:15:58,854 --> 00:16:01,565
Jinman showed me the messages
that he got from the mole.

173
00:16:02,858 --> 00:16:06,529
[♪ pensive music playing]

174
00:16:16,497 --> 00:16:19,208
[Pasin] Once I got into Korea,
I went to that address

175
00:16:20,334 --> 00:16:21,585
and got ambushed.

176
00:16:24,755 --> 00:16:25,756
Pasin?

177
00:16:28,050 --> 00:16:29,427
-[Pasin groans]
-[Brother chuckles softly]

178
00:16:31,012 --> 00:16:35,266
[Jian] My uncle goes missing in Thailand,
and Master Pasin gets ambushed here.

179
00:16:35,891 --> 00:16:38,019
And the two of them never even met up.

180
00:16:39,061 --> 00:16:41,480
What about the message master received,
is it legit?

181
00:16:41,564 --> 00:16:43,733
There are only a few people
who know the random combinations

182
00:16:43,816 --> 00:16:46,068
and to change the e-mail every 12 hours.

183
00:16:46,152 --> 00:16:49,655
Captain Jinman, the mole,
and then just us.

184
00:16:51,240 --> 00:16:53,242
And unless someone in here leaked it,

185
00:16:53,326 --> 00:16:56,037
there's no way the information
we're getting is compromised.

186
00:16:58,748 --> 00:17:01,667
[sighs] Why can't I get in touch
with my uncle, then?
STYLE
::cue()

187
00:17:10,092 --> 00:17:13,012
[♪ tense music playing]

188
00:17:22,313 --> 00:17:25,191
Huh? What's up? You all right?

189
00:17:25,274 --> 00:17:26,650
You should rest longer.

190
00:17:27,360 --> 00:17:28,778
This won't kill me.

191
00:17:30,863 --> 00:17:32,448
You just scan your hand here?

192
00:17:32,573 --> 00:17:34,950
Ah. Wanna go up there?

193
00:17:49,715 --> 00:17:52,301
Officer Jinwoo,
you're still working at the station?

194
00:17:52,385 --> 00:17:54,679
Actually, I quit the police for now.

195
00:17:54,762 --> 00:17:56,097
[chuckles]

196
00:17:58,349 --> 00:17:59,934
You should just stay there.

197
00:18:01,268 --> 00:18:02,728
It suits you better.

198
00:18:04,689 --> 00:18:09,193
After being ambushed by Babylon,
seems like a bitter fit for me here.

199
00:18:10,027 --> 00:18:12,488
And I should stay where I'm needed,
don't you think?

200
00:18:13,864 --> 00:18:17,118
I was just… wasting away.

201
00:18:17,743 --> 00:18:20,871
A police station out in the sticks?
Nothing happens out there.

202
00:18:22,748 --> 00:18:25,084
[♪ tense music continues]

203
00:18:30,548 --> 00:18:34,385
This was actually a grain dryer.
Brother turned it into an elevator.

204
00:18:35,219 --> 00:18:37,722
[Jinwoo] That little punk keeps evolving
down in the basement.

205
00:18:51,736 --> 00:18:53,863
You wouldn't believe what we went through.

206
00:18:53,946 --> 00:18:55,948
It was hell getting this place
up and running.

207
00:18:58,367 --> 00:19:00,828
Code Reds and Code Yellows
really helped us out.

208
00:19:00,911 --> 00:19:02,455
Couldn't have done it without them.

209
00:19:05,624 --> 00:19:08,961
We open the doors at 10:00
and close at 1900.

210
00:19:09,044 --> 00:19:12,673
And then everyone goes home.
Quiet, not a single person's here.

211
00:19:12,757 --> 00:19:14,383
It's perfect for what we're doing.

212
00:19:16,969 --> 00:19:20,639
[Pasin] Everyone here,
are they all civilians?

213
00:19:20,723 --> 00:19:22,558
It covers for us, for sure.

214
00:19:23,517 --> 00:19:25,060
No one would suspect it.

215
00:19:26,270 --> 00:19:27,313
[visitor] President Park!

216
00:19:28,397 --> 00:19:31,192
-Hi, President Choi. How are you?
-Could you come over here?

217
00:19:32,860 --> 00:19:35,863
[Jinwoo] Hey, I'm the president.
I'll be back.

218
00:19:37,573 --> 00:19:40,493
President Choi,
you're coming by so early again.

219
00:19:42,077 --> 00:19:43,579
You're killing me here, really!

220
00:19:44,789 --> 00:19:47,166
[staff] I'll look at it later.
I'll look at it later.

221
00:19:47,249 --> 00:19:49,335
No, no, no.
I'll look at it later, all right?

222
00:19:53,047 --> 00:19:54,048
Oh?

223
00:19:55,132 --> 00:19:57,968
[in Thai] Are you Thai? Eat some of this.

224
00:19:58,636 --> 00:20:02,056
It's not as good as the one back home,
but we can eat it well enough.

225
00:20:02,765 --> 00:20:03,766
I'm fine.

226
00:20:03,849 --> 00:20:06,393
Pasin, why are you standing there
like an idiot?

227
00:20:06,477 --> 00:20:08,020
Take this and go to the toilet.

228
00:20:10,689 --> 00:20:11,941
Babylon is watching everything.

229
00:20:12,024 --> 00:20:16,612
If you want to keep Atti alive,
don't try any funny business. Take it.

230
00:20:16,695 --> 00:20:18,697
[in English] Thanks for everything, man.

231
00:20:20,699 --> 00:20:23,369
[♪ music warping]

232
00:20:37,758 --> 00:20:40,094
[faucet running]

233
00:21:08,414 --> 00:21:09,456
You take a shit?

234
00:21:10,416 --> 00:21:11,917
Why'd you disappear like that?

235
00:21:16,589 --> 00:21:19,466
Don't worry too much about Atti.
Nothing's gonna happen.

236
00:21:20,718 --> 00:21:23,721
Make a full recovery first.
Then you can find him.

237
00:21:24,513 --> 00:21:27,516
[♪ tense pensive music playing]
STYLE
::cue()

238
00:22:04,887 --> 00:22:08,057
Master! Are you feeling better?

239
00:22:08,724 --> 00:22:12,645
-Anything on Jinman?
-No. Not yet.

240
00:22:13,604 --> 00:22:15,481
How about the mole? Anything?

241
00:22:21,320 --> 00:22:24,323
[♪ ominous music playing]

242
00:22:46,428 --> 00:22:48,389
[Brother] Want to go down
to the shopping mall?

243
00:22:50,057 --> 00:22:54,979
Unlike going to the outside,
you need one other thing to get in there.

244
00:23:00,150 --> 00:23:01,610
[machine beeping]

245
00:23:11,286 --> 00:23:14,748
The shopping mall has gotten twice as big.

246
00:23:14,832 --> 00:23:20,087
That also means twice as much work,
but Jinwoo and Jeong Jian help out a lot.

247
00:23:20,170 --> 00:23:23,424
Here I don't even have
to drive a forklift.

248
00:23:24,133 --> 00:23:27,386
If something goes wrong,
is there an escape route?

249
00:23:33,892 --> 00:23:35,144
Of course there is.

250
00:23:36,061 --> 00:23:39,732
But the location is a secret
that only the security manager knows.

251
00:23:40,482 --> 00:23:43,152
Because until recently,
a fake murthehelp app was out there.

252
00:23:43,235 --> 00:23:45,738
The… the dumbass with the stutter is…

253
00:23:47,156 --> 00:23:48,407
that one, isn't he?

254
00:23:48,490 --> 00:23:50,659
[Brother] We lost a lot of clients
because of them,

255
00:23:50,743 --> 00:23:52,828
but we got a lot of them back now.

256
00:23:54,621 --> 00:23:57,875
[♪ tense pensive music playing]

257
00:23:58,876 --> 00:24:00,252
Oh.

258
00:24:02,171 --> 00:24:03,172
Check this out.

259
00:24:04,381 --> 00:24:05,841
Jeong Jian. [chuckles]

260
00:24:05,924 --> 00:24:08,719
Uh… My butt gets sweaty
so she got this for me.

261
00:24:10,137 --> 00:24:12,306
It feels cool. It's nice and dry.

262
00:24:14,141 --> 00:24:17,686
Murthehelp looks like a tight operation
that's so thorough,

263
00:24:17,770 --> 00:24:19,313
then you see things like this.

264
00:24:19,396 --> 00:24:21,440
[Brother] She even bought me two,
in case I need one later.

265
00:24:21,523 --> 00:24:24,068
It's just a gaggle of freaks
that are in there.

266
00:24:24,151 --> 00:24:26,528
[Brother] But she still treats me
like a kid.

267
00:24:26,612 --> 00:24:29,073
[Jin] Is this stuttering fool
really the brains?

268
00:24:30,324 --> 00:24:31,575
Should I just kill him?

269
00:24:36,955 --> 00:24:38,332
[sighs]

270
00:24:38,791 --> 00:24:42,920
How many times do I have to tell you?
Don't you know how to knock?

271
00:24:43,003 --> 00:24:46,090
Oh, I did.
I just didn't hear an answer, so I…

272
00:24:47,257 --> 00:24:49,676
I'll make sure
that I knock louder next time, miss.

273
00:24:52,513 --> 00:24:53,514
Why are you here?

274
00:24:53,597 --> 00:24:58,602
Uh, I'm here about the bus explosion.
Shouldn't we investigate it?

275
00:25:02,231 --> 00:25:04,733
I was looking over the victims'
families' insurance claims

276
00:25:04,817 --> 00:25:06,068
and I started thinking…

277
00:25:06,819 --> 00:25:09,738
it could've been an attack on us
from Jeong Jinman's side.

278
00:25:09,822 --> 00:25:12,407
In that case,
I think we should make preparations.

279
00:25:12,491 --> 00:25:15,369
We should have some contingencies.

280
00:25:15,452 --> 00:25:18,205
Things like this shouldn't happen here,
isn't that right?

281
00:25:18,288 --> 00:25:24,044
Babylon's image is at risk, and it's just,
the employees are feeling really anxious.

282
00:25:24,128 --> 00:25:26,839
The audit team is still investigating, no?

283
00:25:27,965 --> 00:25:29,591
[Inseop] Yes, well, that's true, but…

284
00:25:31,969 --> 00:25:33,679
Then let's just wait a bit longer.

285
00:25:34,930 --> 00:25:37,015
Preparedness is a constant state.

286
00:25:37,099 --> 00:25:39,977
I just think there's too much delay in…

287
00:25:41,186 --> 00:25:42,312
Uh… Never mind, yeah.

288
00:25:44,481 --> 00:25:45,983
Okay. Should I leave?

289
00:25:58,871 --> 00:26:01,290
Should we take care of that idiot lawyer?

290
00:26:02,249 --> 00:26:04,918
He believes that Jeong Jinman was
the one who attacked us.

291
00:26:06,253 --> 00:26:07,421
I wouldn't worry about it.

292
00:26:07,838 --> 00:26:09,548
[scoffs] I guess.

293
00:26:11,008 --> 00:26:13,886
That lawyer's brain couldn't even
comprehend what went on.

294
00:26:15,762 --> 00:26:18,348
That the reason the bus exploded
that night…

295
00:26:18,974 --> 00:26:22,561
[chuckles] …was to cover up
Bale killing Jun.
STYLE
::cue()

296
00:26:33,989 --> 00:26:40,495
Pasin, when we find Atti
and when President Jinman comes back,

297
00:26:42,414 --> 00:26:46,210
can't we all live here together again?

298
00:26:47,878 --> 00:26:51,590
I think it would be… would be nice.

299
00:26:58,972 --> 00:27:00,057
[scoffs]

300
00:27:04,895 --> 00:27:06,855
[♪ ominous music playing]

301
00:27:10,192 --> 00:27:11,818
[Jinman panting]

302
00:27:16,031 --> 00:27:17,741
[mercenary] Mr. Jeong Jinman!

303
00:27:23,330 --> 00:27:25,165
Thanks to you, Mr. Jinman,

304
00:27:25,248 --> 00:27:28,251
Kuma and my team were taken out,
and I got transferred here…

305
00:27:29,169 --> 00:27:30,212
where it's hot as hell.

306
00:27:32,047 --> 00:27:33,173
Ah…

307
00:27:34,216 --> 00:27:36,134
Jo Seonggu, the team leader.

308
00:27:36,551 --> 00:27:38,595
Oh… Thought you forgot.

309
00:27:39,554 --> 00:27:40,555
Well, shoot…

310
00:27:41,306 --> 00:27:43,642
So tell me, Jinman,
why'd you wage a damn war

311
00:27:43,725 --> 00:27:44,977
with Babylon and start this shit?

312
00:27:45,352 --> 00:27:47,646
[groans] Babylon struck first.

313
00:27:48,730 --> 00:27:50,065
I didn't start it.

314
00:27:50,148 --> 00:27:52,442
Makes no difference who started it…

315
00:27:53,902 --> 00:27:57,072
you don't just jump into a battle
you have no chance of winning.

316
00:27:59,032 --> 00:28:03,662
You know, you should've just gone
with the flow. Just like a tree.

317
00:28:04,413 --> 00:28:06,707
If the wind starts blowing,
then you should sway.

318
00:28:07,499 --> 00:28:09,960
Otherwise, you end up taking
the damn beating.

319
00:28:10,877 --> 00:28:12,087
Yeah?

320
00:28:12,170 --> 00:28:17,634
Or else, you'll find yourself like this.
Understand?

321
00:28:20,429 --> 00:28:22,597
-Jo Seonggu.
-What?

322
00:28:23,348 --> 00:28:24,391
Just shut up.

323
00:28:26,059 --> 00:28:28,895
Tell me where Atti is now, I'm in a rush.

324
00:28:30,564 --> 00:28:35,318
Then… I won't kill you
for old times' sake.

325
00:28:41,575 --> 00:28:45,704
Oh, fuck me.
I was about to shit my pants and tell you.

326
00:28:46,997 --> 00:28:48,331
[sighs]

327
00:28:48,665 --> 00:28:49,916
Hey, Jeong Jinman…

328
00:28:51,418 --> 00:28:54,171
you have no idea
what's going on right now, do you?

329
00:28:55,589 --> 00:28:56,757
Just wait a little bit.

330
00:28:57,591 --> 00:29:02,054
I will show you exactly what will happen
to your precious niece and murthehelp.

331
00:29:02,512 --> 00:29:03,972
It's all about to go down.

332
00:29:07,017 --> 00:29:08,560
I hope you're not in pain yet.

333
00:29:09,311 --> 00:29:12,564
Uh-huh. 'Cause from here on,
there's gonna be a lot.

334
00:29:13,815 --> 00:29:15,317
[Seonggu grunts]

335
00:29:16,443 --> 00:29:19,154
[blows thudding]

336
00:29:24,576 --> 00:29:27,454
[Jian] Are we sure they're keeping
Pasin's son in that van?

337
00:29:28,038 --> 00:29:29,331
We never got a picture.

338
00:29:29,414 --> 00:29:33,210
Then that would mean
the mole gave us some false information.

339
00:29:35,128 --> 00:29:36,379
[Pasin] I'll go and handle it.

340
00:29:37,923 --> 00:29:40,300
You need to recover,
you shouldn't go anywhere.

341
00:29:41,885 --> 00:29:43,553
We don't even know if it's accurate.

342
00:29:43,637 --> 00:29:46,973
I have to confirm it. I have to go there.

343
00:29:47,891 --> 00:29:51,269
You guys should… find Jinman quickly.

344
00:29:52,229 --> 00:29:53,230
You should hurry.

345
00:29:55,482 --> 00:29:56,858
If it's to confirm it,

346
00:29:57,818 --> 00:30:00,487
-I think I should go instead.
-Eonni.

347
00:30:00,570 --> 00:30:02,739
[Cheolseung] I don't think
any of us should leave.

348
00:30:02,823 --> 00:30:06,785
It's not a good idea, especially
with the captain missing right now.

349
00:30:07,369 --> 00:30:10,247
Wouldn't it be better to just recruit
a few Code Reds instead?

350
00:30:11,039 --> 00:30:12,040
No.

351
00:30:12,124 --> 00:30:13,750
At the negotiations, they helped us,

352
00:30:13,834 --> 00:30:16,128
but we can't assume
they're on our side yet.

353
00:30:16,211 --> 00:30:17,254
It's too dangerous.

354
00:30:17,337 --> 00:30:20,590
If we move too quickly
and they find out we don't have Jinman,

355
00:30:21,174 --> 00:30:23,593
-they might betray us.
-We're out of time now.

356
00:30:23,677 --> 00:30:24,678
Wait!

357
00:30:27,931 --> 00:30:30,058
The rest of us will hold
the fort down here.

358
00:30:30,767 --> 00:30:33,770
Minhye Eonni can go with Master,
couldn't you?

359
00:30:34,437 --> 00:30:36,773
I think it's too dangerous
to move alone right now.

360
00:30:47,325 --> 00:30:49,578
[K] The shopping mall
is on basement level 2.
STYLE
::cue()

361
00:30:49,661 --> 00:30:53,331
They installed cameras operating with
motion sensors throughout the whole area.

362
00:30:53,915 --> 00:30:56,376
If an intruder is detected,
the alarm goes off

363
00:30:56,459 --> 00:30:58,879
and the entire security system activates.

364
00:31:00,797 --> 00:31:02,507
[Jin] He's one crafty bastard.

365
00:31:03,133 --> 00:31:05,927
He knows how we prefer
to keep our operations covert.

366
00:31:07,429 --> 00:31:10,473
He knows that public exposure
would derail our missions.

367
00:31:12,142 --> 00:31:15,312
That's why he built the shopping mall
beneath a site

368
00:31:16,396 --> 00:31:18,565
that's completely full of civilians.

369
00:31:18,648 --> 00:31:20,317
Is this the only exit?

370
00:31:21,026 --> 00:31:22,277
There's no other way out?

371
00:31:22,360 --> 00:31:24,237
That's the only one that we could find.

372
00:31:25,238 --> 00:31:29,034
[Jin] Once our Thai friend does his job
and eliminates So Minhye,

373
00:31:29,117 --> 00:31:30,702
the shopping mall will be ours.

374
00:31:30,785 --> 00:31:33,914
And they'll be defenseless
except for their internal security system.

375
00:31:33,997 --> 00:31:35,707
And Jeong Jinman's where?

376
00:31:37,209 --> 00:31:38,335
Do we know where he is?

377
00:31:38,418 --> 00:31:41,796
Thailand.
We got confirmation of his entry.

378
00:31:42,464 --> 00:31:45,967
We're currently tracking him down
with help from the Thai branch.

379
00:31:46,551 --> 00:31:48,929
[♪ tense plotting music playing]

380
00:31:49,512 --> 00:31:53,683
Once you have Jeong Jian,
that bastard will have no other choice.

381
00:31:53,767 --> 00:31:55,727
Jeong Jinman will come for her.

382
00:31:56,895 --> 00:31:58,146
It's only a matter of time.

383
00:32:01,650 --> 00:32:04,569
-Is it just the four of us going?
-[Jin] No.

384
00:32:04,653 --> 00:32:06,613
Considering our previous attempt…

385
00:32:08,698 --> 00:32:12,160
for this mission,
I will be assigning two teams.

386
00:32:27,717 --> 00:32:30,679
Are you not gonna tell Q
that we already caught Jeong Jinman?

387
00:32:32,389 --> 00:32:34,641
Don't say anything until we catch her.

388
00:32:35,517 --> 00:32:38,603
We need Q to believe
that Jeong Jinman killed J.

389
00:32:39,104 --> 00:32:42,899
She'll put everything
into capturing Jeong Jian. Pow.

390
00:32:44,067 --> 00:32:45,777
[pants and gasps]

391
00:32:46,945 --> 00:32:49,155
[strained grunt]

392
00:32:58,790 --> 00:33:00,750
[groans in pained effort]

393
00:33:05,463 --> 00:33:07,757
[labored panting]

394
00:33:10,343 --> 00:33:12,512
[grunts, pants]

395
00:33:17,100 --> 00:33:18,768
[clanging]

396
00:33:20,270 --> 00:33:21,604
[in Thai] Fuck! Damn!

397
00:33:22,314 --> 00:33:24,274
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

398
00:33:27,736 --> 00:33:29,112
[distant rapid gunfire]

399
00:33:31,740 --> 00:33:34,117
[guns cock]

400
00:33:34,909 --> 00:33:36,911
[gunfire]

401
00:33:41,583 --> 00:33:43,001
[gunfire]

402
00:33:46,796 --> 00:33:47,797
[in English] Go.

403
00:33:54,179 --> 00:33:56,348
[gunfire]

404
00:33:58,183 --> 00:34:01,061
[gunman groaning, screaming]

405
00:34:01,394 --> 00:34:02,687
-[knife slashing]
-[screaming stops]

406
00:34:03,605 --> 00:34:04,898
[Seonggu clicks tongue]

407
00:34:14,449 --> 00:34:17,243
[gunfire]

408
00:34:17,702 --> 00:34:19,245
[Seonggu groans]

409
00:34:20,246 --> 00:34:22,582
[♪ suspenseful music continues]

410
00:34:28,797 --> 00:34:31,174
[screams in pain]

411
00:34:33,385 --> 00:34:34,677
Where are you holding Atti?

412
00:34:36,554 --> 00:34:38,556
I ain't saying shit to you,
you dumb mother--

413
00:34:38,723 --> 00:34:41,309
[Seonggu screams in pain]

414
00:34:50,360 --> 00:34:52,070
You can't kill me, I said where--
STYLE
::cue()

415
00:35:18,722 --> 00:35:20,974
[birds screeching]

416
00:35:36,364 --> 00:35:38,450
[♪ tense music playing]

417
00:36:24,412 --> 00:36:25,413
[♪ music fades]

418
00:36:32,420 --> 00:36:34,088
[Pasin] That's where they're holding Atti.

419
00:36:37,717 --> 00:36:39,093
[sighs]

420
00:36:40,637 --> 00:36:42,347
So from here, I'll go on foot.

421
00:36:43,723 --> 00:36:47,018
I'll circle to the back and fire a shot
to draw them in.

422
00:36:48,520 --> 00:36:50,730
After the shot, wait one minute.

423
00:36:50,814 --> 00:36:53,441
Then you hit them from the side
and start the rescue.

424
00:36:59,531 --> 00:37:00,532
Pasin…

425
00:37:02,325 --> 00:37:04,077
I swear, I'll rescue Atti.

426
00:37:07,789 --> 00:37:08,790
[Pasin] Yeah.

427
00:37:10,583 --> 00:37:11,584
Minhye…

428
00:37:14,587 --> 00:37:16,047
thank you for everything.

429
00:37:36,317 --> 00:37:37,652
[phone buzzing]

430
00:37:41,322 --> 00:37:43,408
JIAN - I'M UNEASY ABOUT NOT BEING ABLE
TO REACH MY UNCLE.

431
00:37:43,491 --> 00:37:44,492
YOU BE CAREFUL TOO, MINHYE.

432
00:37:44,576 --> 00:37:46,202
[truck engine revving]

433
00:37:46,286 --> 00:37:48,371
[crashing]

434
00:37:48,454 --> 00:37:50,498
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

435
00:37:54,294 --> 00:37:55,587
[grunts]

436
00:37:57,380 --> 00:37:59,340
[tires screeching]

437
00:38:06,306 --> 00:38:08,182
[grunting, panting]

438
00:38:08,266 --> 00:38:10,143
-[gunshots]
-[glass shatters]

439
00:38:13,605 --> 00:38:15,231
[gasps]

440
00:38:15,815 --> 00:38:17,275
[gunshots]

441
00:38:17,400 --> 00:38:18,943
[groans]

442
00:38:23,197 --> 00:38:25,491
[Minhye grunting]
STYLE
::cue()

443
00:38:32,040 --> 00:38:33,416
[Minhye] Pasin…

444
00:38:39,255 --> 00:38:41,549
[gunshots]

445
00:39:09,535 --> 00:39:12,080
[♪ lingering tense music playing]

446
00:39:20,421 --> 00:39:21,923
[line ringing]

447
00:39:23,841 --> 00:39:25,843
I took care of Minhye.

448
00:39:27,887 --> 00:39:31,474
Now… I'll go to the shopping mall.

449
00:39:42,944 --> 00:39:43,945
[♪ music fades]

450
00:40:09,470 --> 00:40:11,097
[lock clanging]

451
00:40:16,436 --> 00:40:18,813
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

452
00:40:28,614 --> 00:40:30,324
[guns cock]

453
00:40:38,166 --> 00:40:40,001
I hired three black-hat hackers

454
00:40:40,084 --> 00:40:43,921
and secured the e-mails exchanged
between Jeong Jinman and his informant.

455
00:40:44,005 --> 00:40:46,174
-[Jin] Do they have what it takes?
-[announcer] Seven, seven.

456
00:40:46,257 --> 00:40:49,469
[K] Yes. They even hacked the NIS before.

457
00:40:49,552 --> 00:40:52,930
[announcer] One-one-zero, one-zero-six…

458
00:40:54,599 --> 00:40:57,268
nine-three, five-zero,

459
00:40:58,978 --> 00:40:59,979
six-nine…

460
00:41:00,563 --> 00:41:02,315
[phone buzzing]

461
00:41:05,610 --> 00:41:06,611
Speak.

462
00:41:10,865 --> 00:41:11,908
Jeong Jinman left?

463
00:41:11,991 --> 00:41:14,452
[yells] Fuck!

464
00:41:14,535 --> 00:41:16,579
[panting]

465
00:41:16,662 --> 00:41:20,291
Tell our Thai branch we need everyone
to prioritize capturing Jeong Jinman.

466
00:41:24,003 --> 00:41:27,131
Q needs to start the mission right away.
We're out of time now.

467
00:41:28,091 --> 00:41:29,092
Tick-tock.

468
00:41:30,093 --> 00:41:31,094
Right away.

469
00:41:32,553 --> 00:41:34,013
[sighs]

470
00:41:34,972 --> 00:41:37,558
-Should I go alone?
-You go ahead.

471
00:41:38,851 --> 00:41:39,894
I'm gonna eat first.
STYLE
::cue()

472
00:41:59,413 --> 00:42:02,416
Jian! Jinman's location was sent to us!

473
00:42:05,461 --> 00:42:09,090
You know how, right? The name
and the passport number all match.

474
00:42:09,173 --> 00:42:12,718
You sure
this is actually the mole's message?

475
00:42:13,511 --> 00:42:16,472
Hey, I thought I told you earlier,
only we know the mole's method to…

476
00:42:16,556 --> 00:42:17,557
Look at this.

477
00:42:18,766 --> 00:42:21,894
These are the e-mails the mole sent
my uncle over the past year.

478
00:42:23,062 --> 00:42:24,730
At the end of every subject line…

479
00:42:29,360 --> 00:42:30,570
they put this here.

480
00:42:31,988 --> 00:42:34,282
I think the mole hid it. Now look.

481
00:42:36,033 --> 00:42:38,536
[♪ tense pensive music playing]

482
00:42:41,539 --> 00:42:42,915
They stop here.

483
00:42:52,758 --> 00:42:54,635
[exhales heavily]

484
00:42:54,719 --> 00:42:56,846
It was right in front of us
this whole time.

485
00:42:56,929 --> 00:43:00,558
The last one with the mark was sent
a week ago.

486
00:43:00,641 --> 00:43:04,270
Babylon assholes somehow intercepted it.

487
00:43:21,704 --> 00:43:22,747
Pasin?

488
00:43:23,956 --> 00:43:26,709
What happened? Did you find Atti?

489
00:43:26,792 --> 00:43:28,085
Where is Minhye?

490
00:43:31,047 --> 00:43:32,548
[Jinwoo grunting]

491
00:43:33,549 --> 00:43:35,635
[rhythmic tapping]

492
00:43:42,600 --> 00:43:45,770
[♪ tense music playing]

493
00:43:53,361 --> 00:43:55,279
BABYLON KIDNAPPED PASIN.
POSSIBLE PASIN IS NOW A DOUBLE AGENT.

494
00:43:58,532 --> 00:43:59,742
[Cheolseung] Thai comrade…

495
00:44:01,244 --> 00:44:02,411
what's going on, man?

496
00:44:02,495 --> 00:44:03,621
Are you doing all right?

497
00:44:06,040 --> 00:44:07,041
Where's Minhye?

498
00:44:09,043 --> 00:44:11,837
Master, please tell me.

499
00:44:13,214 --> 00:44:15,007
What'd you do with my uncle and Minhye?

500
00:44:18,219 --> 00:44:20,638
-Jian, get out of here.
-Master!

501
00:44:23,557 --> 00:44:25,059
[Jian groans]

502
00:44:26,143 --> 00:44:27,520
Get the hell out of here!

503
00:44:27,603 --> 00:44:28,896
[Cheolseung groans]

504
00:44:30,273 --> 00:44:31,774
[Jian groans]

505
00:44:34,485 --> 00:44:36,237
[♪ intense suspenseful music playing]

506
00:44:36,320 --> 00:44:37,321
[Jian groans]

507
00:44:38,990 --> 00:44:40,241
[screams]

508
00:44:43,869 --> 00:44:45,955
-[Cheolseung yells]
-[grunting]

509
00:44:55,589 --> 00:44:57,967
[Jian panting]

510
00:44:59,510 --> 00:45:01,846
[both grunting]

511
00:45:04,682 --> 00:45:05,850
[groans]

512
00:45:08,519 --> 00:45:09,687
[grunts]

513
00:45:19,822 --> 00:45:22,283
[♪ intense suspenseful music continues]

514
00:45:32,084 --> 00:45:33,711
[both grunting]

515
00:45:33,794 --> 00:45:35,504
[groans]

516
00:45:35,713 --> 00:45:37,089
[Cheolseung yells]

517
00:45:45,473 --> 00:45:46,474
[♪ music ends]

518
00:45:59,445 --> 00:46:01,030
[device beeps]

519
00:46:03,324 --> 00:46:04,992
[computer beeping]

520
00:46:07,453 --> 00:46:10,581
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

521
00:46:13,000 --> 00:46:14,960
[panting]
STYLE
::cue()

522
00:46:17,880 --> 00:46:18,923
What?

523
00:46:20,299 --> 00:46:22,134
[error beeping]

524
00:46:22,301 --> 00:46:24,261
[slams lock]

525
00:46:28,641 --> 00:46:29,642
[Brother] What's…?

526
00:46:43,197 --> 00:46:45,032
[grunts in frustration]

527
00:46:51,330 --> 00:46:53,874
[♪ suspenseful music continues]

528
00:47:00,214 --> 00:47:01,465
Jinwoo?

529
00:47:02,591 --> 00:47:03,843
Cheolseung?

530
00:47:04,802 --> 00:47:06,846
Jeong Jian, where are you?

531
00:47:08,055 --> 00:47:10,057
Pasin's turned on us. We have to go!

532
00:47:10,141 --> 00:47:11,684
What did you say?

533
00:47:11,767 --> 00:47:14,437
There's no time.
I'll explain later. We have to go!

534
00:47:18,023 --> 00:47:21,193
[♪ suspenseful music continues]

535
00:47:31,787 --> 00:47:33,581
Pasin, what are you doing?

536
00:47:33,664 --> 00:47:35,499
[screams] Damn it, Master, what the hell?

537
00:47:49,054 --> 00:47:50,764
Jian…

538
00:47:52,766 --> 00:47:55,978
once you pull out your gun,
you just shoot it, all right?

539
00:47:56,979 --> 00:47:59,064
[Jian yelps, groans]

540
00:48:01,066 --> 00:48:03,944
-Brother! Brother! Brother!
-[Brother groans]

541
00:48:06,780 --> 00:48:07,865
[Jian] Pasin!

542
00:48:09,033 --> 00:48:11,827
Please, what are you doing? Please!

543
00:48:17,249 --> 00:48:20,419
[♪ menacing music playing]

544
00:48:30,137 --> 00:48:31,388
[Jin] Watch carefully.

545
00:48:34,934 --> 00:48:39,271
First, the king,
we separate him from the amateur queen.

546
00:48:40,272 --> 00:48:46,362
Then we take their knight
and turn him into ours, just like this.

547
00:48:46,445 --> 00:48:49,031
And send him in like a Trojan horse.

548
00:48:49,114 --> 00:48:51,909
As for the bishops and pawns
who lost their knight,

549
00:48:51,992 --> 00:48:54,036
just steamroll the whole lot.

550
00:49:02,545 --> 00:49:03,546
[beeping]

551
00:49:06,340 --> 00:49:09,593
Both of the units have been docked.
Initiating the hack.

552
00:49:11,387 --> 00:49:12,638
Thanks for working hard.

553
00:49:15,599 --> 00:49:16,809
[in Japanese] What's the situation?

554
00:49:16,892 --> 00:49:19,603
[in English] We've taken control
of their entire security system now.

555
00:49:19,687 --> 00:49:21,355
We only need to move in.

556
00:49:21,438 --> 00:49:24,942
[in Japanese] Tell Q to eliminate Pasin
once Jeong Jian is captured.

557
00:49:28,237 --> 00:49:30,447
[in English] Then, we go in there…

558
00:49:32,157 --> 00:49:33,284
and capture the queen.

559
00:49:34,285 --> 00:49:36,453
[♪ menacing music continues]

560
00:49:39,957 --> 00:49:44,336
Q, driven by pure revenge,
will capture Jeong Jian.

561
00:49:45,004 --> 00:49:46,630
And once we've taken the queen…

562
00:49:51,302 --> 00:49:54,346
the king is put in endgame.

563
00:49:54,430 --> 00:49:59,226
A SHOP FOR KILLERS 2

564
00:50:00,144 --> 00:50:01,145
[♪ music ends]

565
00:50:18,495 --> 00:50:19,955
[Jin] Korean barbecue?

566
00:50:20,164 --> 00:50:22,499
[groans] The smell's gonna stick.

567
00:50:24,251 --> 00:50:25,252
[exhales]

568
00:50:27,004 --> 00:50:29,548
Oh, wow. [chuckles]

569
00:50:31,008 --> 00:50:32,843
I always wanted to meet you in person.

570
00:50:32,926 --> 00:50:34,386
I know it looks shabby, but…

571
00:50:35,471 --> 00:50:39,308
Our meat here is out of this world.
So that's why I invited you.

572
00:50:44,855 --> 00:50:46,065
Hm?

573
00:50:48,025 --> 00:50:51,153
[♪ tense pensive music playing]

574
00:50:55,866 --> 00:50:57,284
Ahn Seongbeom.

575
00:50:58,619 --> 00:50:59,620
It's a pleasure.

576
00:51:02,331 --> 00:51:05,292
[♪ closing theme music playing]

577
00:51:08,170 --> 00:51:09,630
BASED ON THE NOVEL BY KANG JI YOUNG

